claim.claim-text:
train a machine learning classifier based on data from the plurality of animal tag assemblies (102) associated with one or more animals having a known state;
receive data from the plurality of animal tag assemblies (102), the data indicative of two or more animal characteristics of one or more animals of the animal population (150) including (a) at least one physiological characteristic comprising at least one of a temperature or a heart rate, and (b) at least one behavioral characteristic;
assign one or more health states to one or more animals of the animal population (150) with the machine learning classifier based on at least the data received from the plurality of animal tag assemblies (102); and,
report the determined health state to one or more user devices (110).

calculating a temperature metric of the animal for a selected time period, where the temperature metric is indicative of the animal's temperature throughout the selected time period;
calculating an acceleration metric of the animal over the selected time period where the acceleration metric is indicative of the animal's acceleration throughout the selected time period;
determining an average historical temperature metric and an average historical acceleration metric of the animal;
comparing the calculated temperature metric and the calculated acceleration metric to the average historical temperature metric and the average historical acceleration metric to determine the existence of one or more abnormalities; and
wherein the assign one or more health state to one or more animals of the animal population (150) is also based on at least on the one or more abnormalities.
